  (text "CONTROLLER: Pimoroni Pico Plus 2 (RP2350, 16 MB flash, 8 MB PSRAM, USB-C). It has parts underneath, so it plugs into two 20-pin sockets.\nIts USB-C port is the player's only power and data connector: put it on the rear edge of the board.\nPin plan (from docs/DESIGN.md 5.4)\n  GP0-GP7  YM2612 data D0-D7 (PIO, must stay in order)    GP8, GP9  A0, A1    GP10 /WR    GP11 /IC (reset)\n  GP21     7.67 MHz chip clock (GPOUT0: 153.33 MHz / 20)\n  GP14, GP15  I2C1 SDA / SCL to the LCD (through the level shifter on the Front panel page)\n  GP16 Play  GP17 Stop  GP18 Left  GP19 Right  GP20 Edit  GP22 Exit  GP26 Write   (buttons to GND, internal pull-ups)\n  GP27, GP28  data knob A / B\n  GP12, GP13  spare, on J1 (not fitted)\n/RD is tied high and /CS low at the chip, so the bus only ever writes." (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid a9ff56c5-199a-5c04-a6d4-52f9a2eb1861)
  )
  (text "Boot-time pulls: until the firmware starts, these hold the\nYM2612 in reset and keep /WR idle." (at 228.6 220.98 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 16bf9da6-04d2-5329-82d4-e0d4217b1869)
  )
